# Zul Ashur, Lich Lord: "{T}: You may cast target Zombie creature card from your graveyard this turn" (CR 601.3, 611.2a). Bot1 casts
# Zul Ashur, a Walking Corpse (Zombie) and a Grizzly Bears (not a Zombie) on turn 1, and Bot2 kills the Corpse and the Bears with two
# Lightning Bolts on turn 2. So Bot1's graveyard holds the Corpse, the Bears and the sacrificed Black Lotus. On turn 3 Zul Ashur cannot
# target the Bears (a creature card, but not a Zombie) or the Black Lotus (not a creature card at all); it targets the
# Corpse, is tapped and cannot be activated again, and the grant covers only the Corpse (the Bears still cannot be cast). "May": Bot1
# does not cast it and the Corpse stays in the graveyard. On turn 5 the grant is gone (the Corpse cannot be cast); Zul Ashur taps again,
# and now the Corpse is cast from the graveyard and enters the battlefield.

